{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# Vachan V2 spike — Per-Persona Tone Dial (control vector v2)\n\n**What this proves:** instead of a generic Hinglish/English contrast, we build the tone vector *from a real persona's own anchor phrases* — the warm Hinglish voice samples we already store vs. their formal English translations. The result is a vector that points toward **that specific person's** casual voice, not generic Hinglish.\n\n**Why it matters:** Priya's dial is different from Rahul's. Generic Hinglish overshoots for some personas and undershoots for others. Using the persona's own anchors makes the vector match their actual writing style.\n\n**PFS gate built in:** after generating, we measure `av_cosine` against the persona's English centroid (the same metric that already gates Groq). If it falls below the threshold we auto-tune `coeff` — this ties the control vector directly into the Fidelity Ring objective.\n\n> Runtime: ~8–12 min on a Kaggle **T4**. Same model as the basic spike (Llama-3.1-8B in 4-bit)."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 0. Setup\n\n1. Kaggle: **Accelerator → GPU T4**, **Internet → On**.\n2. No HuggingFace token needed (non-gated mirror).\n3. Run cells top to bottom (**Run All**).\n\n**What's different from the basic spike:** the basic spike used two hardcoded system prompts (`POS`/`NEG`). This notebook loads a persona JSON, reads its anchor phrases, and builds the contrastive pairs from those — so the vector is shaped by the persona's actual language patterns."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "!pip install -q repeng transformers accelerate bitsandbytes sentence-transformers"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "import torch, json, numpy as np\nfrom transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer, BitsAndBytesConfig\nfrom repeng import ControlVector, ControlModel, DatasetEntry\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\n\nMODEL = \"NousResearch/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct\"\n\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(MODEL)\ntokenizer.pad_token_id = tokenizer.eos_token_id\n\nbnb = BitsAndBytesConfig(\n    load_in_4bit=True,\n    bnb_4bit_compute_dtype=torch.float16,\n    bnb_4bit_quant_type=\"nf4\",\n)\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(MODEL, quantization_config=bnb, device_map=\"auto\")\nmodel = ControlModel(model, list(range(-5, -18, -1)))\n\n# Embedding model for the PFS cosine gate (same one the Fidelity Ring uses)\nembed_model = SentenceTransformer('all-MiniLM-L6-v2')\n\nprint(\"models loaded:\", MODEL)"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 1. Define a sample persona\n\nIn production this JSON comes from the Vachan persona store. For this spike we embed it inline so the notebook is fully standalone — paste any real persona's anchors here to test."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# Paste any real persona's data here.\n# hinglish_anchors: short phrases this person actually texts (warm, casual voice)\n# english_anchors: formal/English version of the same meaning (the contrast pole)\n# english_centroid_phrases: used to compute the PFS av_cosine gate (same as Fidelity Ring)\nPERSONA = {\n    \"name\": \"Priya\",\n    \"hinglish_anchors\": [\n        \"arre yaar kya hoga ab\",\n        \"haan bhai dekh lete hai\",\n        \"chill kar, sab theek ho jayega\",\n        \"sun, ek kaam kar\",\n        \"theek hai, kar deta/deti hoon\",\n        \"bhai bohot busy tha/thi aaj\",\n        \"kal milte hai okay?\",\n        \"seriously yaar, ye kya tha\",\n    ],\n    \"english_anchors\": [\n        \"What will happen now?\",\n        \"Yes, we will look into it.\",\n        \"Please relax, everything will be fine.\",\n        \"Listen, please do one thing.\",\n        \"Alright, I will take care of it.\",\n        \"I was quite busy today.\",\n        \"Let us meet tomorrow, okay?\",\n        \"Seriously, what was that?\",\n    ],\n    \"english_centroid_phrases\": [\n        \"Please review the attached document.\",\n        \"I will follow up on this tomorrow.\",\n        \"The deployment has been completed successfully.\",\n        \"Let me know if you have any questions.\",\n        \"We will schedule the meeting accordingly.\",\n    ],\n}\nprint(f\"Persona: {PERSONA['name']} | {len(PERSONA['hinglish_anchors'])} anchor pairs loaded\")"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 2. Build contrastive pairs from persona anchors\n\nSame mechanism as the basic spike, but now `positive` = persona's actual Hinglish phrase, `negative` = its English translation. The vector direction we learn points toward *this persona's* natural casual voice, not generic Hinglish."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# Generic suffixes give the model many token positions to read the hidden state from.\n# Combined with persona anchors as the system context, this shapes the vector.\nSUFFIXES = [\n    \"\", \"I\", \"I think\", \"Let me\", \"Sure\", \"Honestly\",\n    \"Okay so\", \"The plan\", \"Yeah\", \"So\",\n]\n\ndef framed_anchor(anchor: str, suffix: str) -> str:\n    msgs = [\n        {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": f\"You are texting like this: '{anchor}'\"},\n        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Give me an update on the project.\"},\n    ]\n    s = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(msgs, tokenize=False, add_generation_prompt=True)\n    return s + suffix\n\ndataset = []\nfor hi, en in zip(PERSONA['hinglish_anchors'], PERSONA['english_anchors']):\n    for suffix in SUFFIXES:\n        dataset.append(DatasetEntry(\n            positive=framed_anchor(hi, suffix),\n            negative=framed_anchor(en, suffix),\n        ))\n\nprint(f\"{len(dataset)} contrastive pairs built from {len(PERSONA['hinglish_anchors'])} anchor pairs × {len(SUFFIXES)} suffixes\")\nprint(\"--- sample positive (tail) ---\")\nprint(dataset[3].positive[-140:])"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 3. Extract the per-persona control vector"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "model.reset()\npersona_vector = ControlVector.train(model, tokenizer, dataset)\n\n_layers = list(persona_vector.directions.keys())\nprint(f\"{PERSONA['name']} persona vector: {len(_layers)} layers, shape {persona_vector.directions[_layers[0]].shape}\")"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 4. PFS cosine gate — tune the dial until Fidelity Ring passes\n\nWe compute `av_cosine` against the persona's English centroid (same metric that gates Groq in Path-A). We sweep `coeff` values and find the highest one where `av_cosine >= PFS_THRESHOLD`. This is the production-safe dial setting for this persona."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "PFS_THRESHOLD = 0.65  # same threshold as the Fidelity Ring gate\nPROMPT = \"Can you give me an update on the deployment?\"\n\n# Pre-compute English centroid embeddings\nen_centroid = embed_model.encode(PERSONA['english_centroid_phrases'], normalize_embeddings=True).mean(axis=0)\n\ndef generate(prompt: str, coeff: float, max_new_tokens: int = 80) -> str:\n    model.reset()\n    if coeff != 0:\n        model.set_control(persona_vector, coeff)\n    msgs = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}]\n    ids = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(msgs, return_tensors=\"pt\", add_generation_prompt=True).to(model.device)\n    out = model.generate(\n        ids,\n        max_new_tokens=max_new_tokens,\n        do_sample=False,\n        repetition_penalty=1.3,\n        pad_token_id=tokenizer.eos_token_id,\n    )\n    model.reset()\n    return tokenizer.decode(out[0, ids.shape[-1]:], skip_special_tokens=True).strip()\n\ndef av_cosine(text: str) -> float:\n    emb = embed_model.encode([text], normalize_embeddings=True)[0]\n    return float(np.dot(emb, en_centroid))\n\n# Sweep from low to high; stop when cosine drops below threshold\nresults = []\nfor coeff in [0.0, 0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5]:\n    resp = generate(PROMPT, coeff)\n    cos = av_cosine(resp)\n    results.append((coeff, cos, resp))\n    status = \"PASS\" if cos >= PFS_THRESHOLD else \"FAIL\"\n    print(f\"coeff {coeff:+.1f} | av_cosine {cos:.3f} [{status}] | {resp[:80]}...\")\n\n# Best coeff = highest coeff that still passes the gate\npassing = [(c, cos, r) for c, cos, r in results if cos >= PFS_THRESHOLD]\nbest_coeff, best_cos, best_resp = max(passing, key=lambda x: x[0]) if passing else (0.0, results[0][1], results[0][2])\nprint(f\"\\n=== Best dial setting: coeff {best_coeff:+.1f} (av_cosine {best_cos:.3f}) ===")"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 5. Full comparison — same prompt, full dial sweep"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "print(f\"\\nPersona: {PERSONA['name']} | PFS threshold: {PFS_THRESHOLD}\\n\")\nfor coeff, cos, resp in results:\n    gate = \"PASS\" if cos >= PFS_THRESHOLD else \"FAIL\"\n    print(f\"--- coeff {coeff:+.1f} | av_cosine {cos:.3f} [{gate}] ---\")\n    print(resp)\n    print()\n\nprint(f\"=== Recommended production coeff for {PERSONA['name']}: {best_coeff} ===")"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 6. Save the vector for reuse"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "import os, pickle\n\nout_dir = f\"/kaggle/working/vectors\"\nos.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\nvec_path = f\"{out_dir}/{PERSONA['name'].lower()}_tone_vector.pkl\"\nwith open(vec_path, 'wb') as f:\n    pickle.dump({\n        'persona': PERSONA['name'],\n        'vector': persona_vector,\n        'best_coeff': best_coeff,\n        'av_cosine_at_best': best_cos,\n        'pfs_threshold': PFS_THRESHOLD,\n    }, f)\n\nprint(f\"Saved: {vec_path}\")\nprint(f\"To reload: pickle.load(open('{vec_path}', 'rb'))\")\nprint(f\"\\nSummary:\")\nprint(f\"  Persona         : {PERSONA['name']}\")\nprint(f\"  Best coeff      : {best_coeff}\")\nprint(f\"  av_cosine       : {best_cos:.3f}\")\nprint(f\"  PFS gate        : {'PASS' if best_cos >= PFS_THRESHOLD else 'FAIL'}\")\nprint(f\"  Vector file     : {vec_path}\")"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 7. What's next\n\n**If the gate passes at coeff > 0:** the persona's voice is steerable with their own anchors. This is the per-persona dial ready for integration.\n\n**If the gate never passes above coeff 0:** the persona's Hinglish anchors aren't distinctive enough — either add more anchor pairs (aim for 12-16), or tighten the contrast (make the English side more formal).\n\n**Path into Vachan (not this notebook):**\n1. Store the vector pkl per-persona in the data layer.\n2. Serve inference behind vLLM/transformers on a serverless GPU — repeng's `ControlModel` hooks into the forward pass.\n3. At call time: load the persona's pkl → set coeff → generate → measure cosine → reset. The Fidelity Ring's av_cosine gate becomes the feedback loop that selects the right coeff live.\n4. Path-B trigger: only activate the control-vector path for personas where Groq is consistently failing the PFS gate (cost stays low; GPU only fires for edge cases)."
  }
 ],
